// @no-instantiate
// THIS IS INVENTORY ROW D7, not a separate defect — `docs/internals/silent-class-inventory.md`
// § "D7 — `xs[0] ?? d` over a nullable-ELEMENT list emits invalid wasm" is the same program
// and the same two silent cells. It was filed in both places under two names. When this
// graduates, RE-GRADE D7 in that file too, or the queue keeps one live row for a fixed
// defect — the failure mode that left eight rows there stale.
// MISCOMPILE, pinned: `??` over a LIST INDEX whose element is `string | null`. `vl check`
// exits 0 with no diagnostic at any severity, `vl build` writes the `.wasm` and reports
// success, and the failure arrives only when something tries to instantiate it —
//
//   type mismatch: expected (ref $type), found (ref null $type)
//
// THE MECHANISM, read off the disassembly rather than guessed. `xs[1] ?? "q"` lowers to an
// if-EXPRESSION whose result type is the NON-NULL string the coalesce promises:
//
//   (if (result (ref $str))
//     (ref.is_null (array.get $back …))     ;; the null test, on a re-read
//     (then (global.get $default))          ;; the default — already non-null
//     (else (array.get $back …)))           ;; THE SAME READ AGAIN, still (ref null $str)
//
// The backing of a `(string | null)[]` is `(array (mut (ref null $str)))`, so the ELSE arm's
// `array.get` yields the NULLABLE reference. Every other `??` sink narrows at this seam; the
// list-index arm re-reads and hands the raw nullable straight to a slot declared non-null.
// The `then` arm is fine, which is why the shape only shows up once the else arm is reached
// by the validator rather than by execution.
//
// FILED, and this file is its witness: `docs/internals/per-rep-ladder-audit.md` §"Residues
// the grid measured and this slice did NOT close" records it as the one check-clean INVALID
// WASM cell of the `??`-over-a-list-index row — "`xs[1] ?? "q"` is `emitProgram: `??` is
// only supported on a map index get` for every litunion spelling (4 cells) and check-clean
// INVALID WASM for the `(string | null)[]` control (1 cell), which is the worse verdict and
// is pre-existing." The four LITUNION spellings are a LOUD emit reject and need no pin; the
// `string | null` control is the one that compiles.
//
// WHY IT LIVES HERE AND NOT BESIDE ITS SUBJECT. `@no-instantiate` is the corpus's marker for
// the check-clean-invalid-wasm class, and `tests/vl_check_codegen_test.ts` asserts SET
// EQUALITY between the files carrying it and the files `vl check --codegen` flags — so the
// class needs at least one live member or that tripwire has nothing to measure. It inherited
// the seat from `std/xfail-miscompile-array-litunion-element.vl`, which graduated when the
// inline-literal-union element family's last two boundaries closed.
//
// WHEN IT IS FIXED this file starts failing (the module instantiates), which is the point.
// The fix is to delete it, fold the program into the `??` coverage beside the map-index
// rows, and give the else arm the same narrow the `then` arm does not need.
const xs = ["p", null]
print(xs[1] ?? "q")
